C MP+relaxed
"The same message-passing shape with RELAXED atomics on the flag. C11 ALLOWS the
 stale-data outcome r0=1 /\ r1=0: relaxed accesses carry no happens-before, so
 the writer's two stores and the reader's two loads may each be observed out of
 order. herd7 -c11 => Sometimes. CRC has NO relaxed accesses in its fragment, so
 this program lies outside CRC's language entirely -- equivalently, CRC's weakest
 atomic (release/acquire, MP+relacq.litmus) forbids the outcome. Thus C11 permits
 a behaviour CRC excludes: CRC is strictly stronger."
{ int x=0; int f=0; }
P0 (atomic_int* x, atomic_int* f) {
  atomic_store_explicit(x,1,memory_order_relaxed);
  atomic_store_explicit(f,1,memory_order_relaxed);
}
P1 (atomic_int* x, atomic_int* f) {
  int r0 = atomic_load_explicit(f,memory_order_relaxed);
  int r1 = atomic_load_explicit(x,memory_order_relaxed);
}
exists (1:r0=1 /\ 1:r1=0)
